\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Why land-derived harmonization fails over clear water. (a) The Roy intercept relative to the native over-water Landsat signal, by band. (b) Accuracy of a classifier predicting the source sensor from harmonized features; under a successful harmonization it would sit at chance. (c) Sentinel-2 versus harmonized Landsat reflectance on the 270{} paired station--date events; blue agrees worst. (d) Median spectral signature before and after local water recalibration; labels are the Landsat/Sentinel-2 ratio.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
